fc-07 complete: the Loam Video / Loam Effects router and a full "Video editing" prompt section. One product, one workflow, Arabic + English routing, FilmCraft-native fallback.

## Fourth validation pass (one real defect fixed: commit `b36a8af`)
Drove the router and the tool envelope through an ad-hoc probe (bilingual inputs,
normalisation, classification, `plan()` degradation, and the real `run()` against a stub
relay with temp dist roots), then swept every string the tool can hand back to the model.

The probe found one genuine branding defect the three earlier passes had waved through as
"machine-readable, therefore fine": the dist-missing fallback envelope returned
`reason: "filmcraft_dist_missing"`, an upstream project name inside the JSON the model reads
and routinely relays to the user. A `git grep` confirmed no frontend consumer parses that
reason, so it is renamed to `loam_video_dist_missing` in the `VideoStudioFallbackReason`
union, at the call site, in the pinned test assertion and in the docs table. The rest of the
tool's user-facing text was already clean: every remaining `filmcraft` occurrence is a doc
comment, an internal identifier (`filmcraftDistDir`, `isFilmcraftDistInstalled`) or the real
vendored path `electron/filmcraft/dist`, and the dist-missing *message* is already branded
("The Loam Video dist is not installed (...)"). The rename is safe against future merges:
`manus-parity` still uses the old spelling, so there is nothing to collide with.

A regression test now pins the class of leak, not just the instance. `video_studio branding`
drives the tool through nine envelopes (dist missing, panel not open, bridge failure,
rejected command, cancelled, missing command, unknown action, success) and asserts no
upstream name appears in any of them, stripping real filesystem paths first so the
legitimate vendored dist location is not miscounted as a leak; it also asserts the reason
codes are brand-neutral. `videoStudio.test.ts` is now 42 tests, 42 pass.

Also verified in this pass:
- Regenerating the master prompt is idempotent: `npm run gen:master-prompt` leaves the
  working tree clean (27 sections), so `masterPromptText.ts` matches `prompts/loam-master.md`.
- The probe corrected several of my own wrong assumptions rather than exposing code defects:
  the tool method is `run(args, ctx)` (from `Tool` in `src/tools/registry.ts`), not
  `execute`; the stub relay must answer the `commands` method with a catalog or the tool
  reports "editor returned no command list"; and `transition_basic` carrying a transition
  hint degrades as `effects_engine_unsupported` when the effects dist is installed but
  `effects_backend_unavailable` when it is missing, exactly as the committed tests pin.
- Both full-suite failures (`node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"`: 2203 tests,
  2201 pass, 2 fail) reproduce identically on the clean `manus-parity` worktree, and both
  files are untouched by fc-07 (`git diff --stat manus-parity` is empty for each), so
  neither is a regression: `src/agent/__tests__/toolDescriptions.test.ts` (the inherited
  `suggest_plan` defect) and `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` "reports non-git
  folders without throwing" (3 pass / 1 fail on `manus-parity` too; `readGitBranch` on a
  fresh temp dir under this machine's git configuration reports `isGit: true`, an
  environment quirk, not a code failure).

Gates re-run on the committed tree (all green):
- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server` -> exit 0 (dist/server.cjs 19.3mb, pdf worker copied)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)` -> exit 0 (compiled successfully, 25/25 static pages)
- `npm run check:encoding` / `check:promptwire` / `check:modes` / `check:loam-agents` -> PASS
- `node --import tsx --test` targeted suites (videoStudio 42, videoStudioRouter 47,
  videoEditAgent 12, videoPrompt 16, codingPrompt 8) -> all pass
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"` -> tests 2203, pass 2201, fail 2 (both
  pre-existing, above)

