## Third validation pass (no new defects)
Re-verified the snapshot and the routing contract end to end, then re-ran every gate.
The earlier `TypeError [ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE]` while recomputing the snapshot hash was
an artifact of importing the wrong export: the module exports `MASTER_PROMPT_SECTIONS`
(an array), not a `masterPromptText` string. Hashing the real assembly
(`buildMasterPrompt(ALL_SLOTS, { model: "qwen2.5:14b" })`, exactly as
`codingPrompt.test.ts` does) reproduces the committed value byte for byte:
`masterPromptSha256 = 80b1235fae56672d72a128d71971a72660c8955699adc6f3c3487b36cd4c34ab`,
`codingSectionSha256 = ef715eb596edf9d39281878ee278a18a64cef025e38f4bbb82d576eeb327249f`
(unchanged). Also confirmed:
- `plan()` is live, not dead code: `src/tools/videoStudio.ts:708` calls
  `router.plan(action, routingHint(args))`. `plan.action` has no consumers, but a
  `git grep` for `\.plan(` shows the only other call sites are the router's own tests.
- Arabic is scoped correctly: 165 Arabic words live only in `videoStudioRouter.ts`
  (the bilingual phrase tables) and 92 only in `prompts/loam-master.md` /
  `masterPromptText.ts` (the §6.12 examples). `videoPrompt.ts`, `prompt.ts` and
  `planner.ts` contain none, so no Arabic leaks into unrelated guidance.
- Branding holds under the real assembly path: `videoPrompt.ts`'s exported strings
  contain zero occurrences of filmcraft/effectcraft/artcraft, and §6.12's body matches
  the generated asset.
- The 237-test gate figure is real, not a phantom: the file list in this report had
  abbreviated the `src/server/` and `src/policy/` prefixes. The actual paths are
  `src/server/__tests__/{videoStudioE2E,videoStudioRelay,autoVideo,runTools}.test.ts`
  and `src/policy/__tests__/riskTier.test.ts`; run individually they total
  40+47+16+21+8+4+8+4+16+73 = 237 tests, 237 pass, 0 fail.
- One unrelated pre-existing failure was found and ruled out of scope:
  `src/agent/__tests__/toolDescriptions.test.ts` fails on `suggest_plan` ("neither
  registered nor listed in PENDING_CODING_TOOLS"). It reproduces identically on the
  clean `manus-parity` worktree, and fc-07 never modified that test or
  `src/agent/toolDescriptions.ts` (both are byte-identical to base), so it is not a
  regression from this task.

## Second validation pass (commit `5579808`)
A third look at the `video_studio` run body found a contract gap the first two passes
missed: the tool description promises "Every result carries a `routing` object", but the
three early returns (missing dist, `panel_not_open`, relay failure) dropped it, so a failed
call told the user nothing about the engine that was chosen. `VideoStudioRouting` is now a
named type, `fallbackResult` and `relayErrorResult` take it, and a regression test pins all
three failure envelopes (including a degraded `effects` request that fails before any
command runs: `route: effects`, `target: film`, `degraded: true`, reason
`effects_backend_unavailable`).
Also verified: `plan.action` never differs from the requested action (0 differences across
every action x hint combination), so the dead field is not a behaviour bug; `raw` validates
its command id against the *target* engine's catalog, so degradation cannot dispatch a
foreign id; and no upstream engine name appears in any user-facing string (all occurrences
are internal identifiers, doc comments, or the pre-existing machine-readable reason code
`filmcraft_dist_missing`, since renamed to `loam_video_dist_missing` in the fourth pass).

## Extra validation pass (commit `c4aa207`)
Beyond the first gates, the router tables were probed directly with ad-hoc bilingual
inputs. That surfaced one real defect: `FALLBACK_TRANSITION_PHRASES` carried a bare
`"slide"`, so "slide in the text" (text/motion animation) was degraded to the timeline
engine's *transition* command instead of its *effect* command. The marker was removed
(the same treatment already applied to bare `"zoom"`, `"glitch"`, `"morph"`), the
doc comment explains why, and a regression test now pins both sides: "slide in the
text" -> `effect_basic`, while an explicit "slide transition" still -> `transition_basic`.
Also verified directly: the generated `masterPromptText.ts` contains §6.12 in Appendix B
order (§6.11 < §6.12 < §7), carries no upstream engine name, and `videoPrompt.ts`'s
`VIDEO_STUDIO_ACTIONS` list is byte-identical to the tool's `action` enum.

## What was produced (commit `2f5c69c`, branch `khamis1992/fc-07` on base `manus-parity`)
1. **Router module** `src/tools/videoStudioRouter.ts` (new). Classifies each requested
   operation into `film` (cut, trim, arrange, speed, audio, music, volume, basic text,
   export) or `effects` (transitions beyond a basic dissolve, visual effects, colour looks,
   text/motion animation, keyframed motion, animated titles). Phrase matching is Latin
   word-boundary + Arabic substring, with Arabic normalisation (harakat/tatweel, alef/yaa/
   taa-marbuta variants, hamza). When the EffectCraft backend is unavailable, an `effects`
   op degrades to FilmCraft-native `transition_basic` / `effect_basic` and the tool says so
   (`plan()` returns the degradation contract, not a failure).
2. **Master prompt section** §6.12 "Video editing (Loam Video + Loam Effects)" added to
   `prompts/loam-master.md` (the source of truth), immediately before `## 7. Parallel Tool
   Calls`. It documents the open -> state -> incremental edits -> verify (state/screenshot)
   -> export loop, the routing split, preserving manual edits, and Arabic examples. Regenerated
   `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts` with `npm run gen:master-prompt` (27 sections).
3. **Gated prompt guidance** `src/agent/videoPrompt.ts` (new), mirroring the §6.11 `craftPrompt.ts`
   pattern: exports the video constants, `VIDEO_EDITING_PROMPT`, and `hasVideoStudioTool()`.
   Wired into `src/agent/prompt.ts` so the section is injected ONLY when `video_studio` is
   registered, plus a Loam Video planner rule in `src/agent/planner.ts` (mirroring the Craft rule).

## Tests (node --import tsx --test)
- `src/tools/__tests__/videoStudioRouter.test.ts` (new, ~500 lines): bilingual classification
  table, normalisation, phrase matching, action routing, availability probes,
  transition-vs-effect fallback, `plan()` degradation contract, branding contract.
- `src/agent/__tests__/videoPrompt.test.ts` (new): guidance injected only for `video_studio`,
  the open->state->edits->verify->export loop, routing/degrade contract, §6.12 in the master
  prompt after §6.11, planner rule, branding.
- Fixed three real table bugs the tests surfaced in `videoStudioRouter.ts`: removed the
  colliding generic words `"motion"` / `"حركي"` / `"حركيه"` from `EFFECTS_PHRASES` (a lone
  "motion" is ambiguous; "slow motion" is film); added `"الوان"` and `"صحح الوان"` to the
  colour table; trimmed `FALLBACK_TRANSITION_PHRASES` to genuine transition markers only
  (dropped bare `"zoom"`, `"glitch"`, `"morph"`, `"متحول"`). Also added natural Arabic film
  phrases (`"قطع"`, `"جمد الاطار"`, `"انشي الفيديو"`/`"انشاء الفيديو"`, `"صدر الفيديو"`).

